### Results Persistence — `result_logger.py`

Every experiment run (baseline, time horizon sweep, GA optimization) will be saved to a structured `RESULTS/` directory so nothing is lost.

#### [NEW] [result_logger.py](file:///c:/Politechnika/Masters/Thesis%20-%202/result_logger.py)

**Folder naming convention:**
```
RESULTS/
  baseline_jpm_20260521_094100/
  ga_features_only_20260521_121530/
  ga_full_tuning_20260521_180200/
  time_horizon_t2_20260521_193000/
```
Pattern: `{experiment_type}_{details}_{YYYYMMDD}_{HHMMSS}`

**Each run folder contains:**

| File | Contents |
|---|---|
| `config.json` | All hyperparameters, feature list, window size, dataset path, mode |
| `metrics.json` | Final test metrics (MSE, RMSE, MAE, R², DA) |
| `training_log.csv` | Per-epoch train/val loss history |
| `ga_history.csv` | *(GA runs only)* Per-generation min/avg/max fitness |
| `best_chromosome.json` | *(GA runs only)* The winning chromosome decoded |
| `model.pt` | Copy of the checkpoint (or symlink) |

**Key class & methods:**
- `ResultLogger.__init__(experiment_name: str, sub_label: str)` — creates the timestamped folder under `RESULTS/`.
- `log_config(config: dict)` — writes `config.json`.
- `log_metrics(metrics: dict)` — writes `metrics.json`.
- `log_epoch(epoch: int, train_loss: float, val_loss: float)` — appends a row to `training_log.csv`.
- `log_ga_generation(gen: int, stats: dict)` — appends a row to `ga_history.csv`.
- `log_best_chromosome(chromosome: dict)` — writes `best_chromosome.json`.
- `copy_checkpoint(src_path: str)` — copies the `.pt` file into the run folder.
- `get_run_dir() -> Path` — returns the absolute path of the current run folder.

**Integration points:**
- `Trainer.train()` will accept an optional `ResultLogger` and call `log_epoch()` each epoch.
- `GAOptimizer.run()` will accept an optional `ResultLogger` and call `log_ga_generation()` each generation.
- `main.py` experiment functions will create a `ResultLogger`, pass it through, and call `log_metrics()` + `copy_checkpoint()` at the end.

